56a86a1d7b26"],

Cell["\<\
From paper: If there is sufficient energy intake, an animal allocates the \
energy obtained in the order: maintenance, growth, reproduction, energy \
storage, until its energy stores reach an optimal level. If there is a \
shortfall, the priorities for maintenance and growth/reproduction remain the \
same until reserves fall to a critical threshold below which all are \
allocated to maintenance. [cite]\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.982253020855629*^9, 3.982253031160576*^9}, {
  3.982255872361162*^9, 3.982256007212734*^9}, {3.982949042916792*^9, 
  3.982949052745554*^9}, {3.988668762843704*^9, 
  3.988668771359005*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"2f6dff15-ac40-5946-9765-\
dfadd688eaf0"]
}, Open  ]]
